[SPOILER='Roadmap - known limitations and planned work in 3.0.0-beta.2']
Rough edges I already know about, with direction:

[LIST]
[*][B]Spigot main-thread fallback[/B] - when the Anvil pre-filter can't resolve a chunk, one on-tick load fills the gap. Planned: per-minute fallback counters and an optional strict mode that skips the fallback entirely.
[*][B]Folia scheduler hop[/B] for un-pre-resolvable candidates - cost currently unmeasured. Planned: publish p50/p95, look at amortising across adjacent candidates.
[*][B]Un-populated chunks[/B] always fall through to a live load (correct by design). Planned: dedicated attribution bucket so operators can distinguish this from other fallbacks.
[*][B]Multi-server / proxy[/B] (Velocity, BungeeCord) - planned for [I]3.0.0-beta.3[/I]. Cross-network UUID queue + reservation tokens in the network-state DB.
[*][B]Fabric[/B] - functional first-class platform (unstable frontier). Stabilization work continues on scheduled-task processor parity, permissions, and full Brigadier tree. Native Forge/NeoForge remains lower priority than multi-server; Arclight/Mohist + the Spigot/Paper jar is the supported path there.
[*][B]Telemetry-sourced marketing numbers.[/B] ~45% Overworld-safe is local-rig profiling; Nether/End are qualitative. Planned: anonymous opt-in telemetry + a published reference benchmark.
[*][B]Demo videos predate this release.[/B] Underlying principles unchanged; numbers aren't current. Planned: fresh footage before [I]-beta[/I] comes off.
[/LIST]

[I]Everything above is a known issue with a plan - not a surprise. If you hit something not on this list, please open a GitHub issue.[/I]
[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER='FAQ']
[B]Q: Why does this respond faster than other RTP plugins?[/B]
A: Pre-warmed queue. In most cases a verified destination is ready before you type [I]/rtp[/I]. Two design choices keep that queue cheap to refill: a [B]persistent spatial memory[/B] per region (the plugin remembers which sectors failed safety checks, so the spiral selector skips known-bad ground instead of rerolling indefinitely) and an [B]off-tick async pre-filter[/B] (Anvil region files are read directly to reject unsafe biomes/blocks [I]before[/I] any chunk is loaded, so candidate verification never blocks the main thread).

[B]Q: How do I set up teleportation between worlds?[/B]
A: See the admin guide. Resolution order: player's current world (or [I]world:[/I] param) -> world's target region -> region's target world.

[B]Q: Iris / Terra / custom datapack generators?[/B]
A: Yes - deliberate 3.0 design goal. The Anvil pre-filter reads [I].mca[/I] palette data directly, so populated custom-generator chunks evaluate off-tick like vanilla. That's [I]strictly more accurate[/I] than the live Bukkit view, which collapses modded IDs to vanilla cousins. Un-populated chunks fall through to a live load as the authoritative safety net.

[B]Q: Existing safety.yml on upgrade?[/B]
A: Plain-material entries keep working unchanged; the new grammar is strictly additive.

[B]Q: Best setup for performance?[/B]
A: Paper, with memory to spare for the location cache. RTP works particularly well on pre-generated worlds.

[B]Q: Can I downgrade to the free RTP build?[/B]
A: Yes - same configuration, same data files, same commands. You lose Folia, proxy, SQL/Redis, Vault, multilingual, and the tag/state-predicate grammar.
[/SPOILER]

