[SPOILER='Support Policy (enforced - read before purchase)']
[LIST]
[*][B]Support covers bugs and configuration questions,[/B] after you've read the admin guide.
[*][B]Bug reports need a reproduction:[/B] server version, plugin version, platform (Spigot/Paper/Folia), [I]config.yml[/I], [I]regions/[/I], [I]safety.yml[/I], and the relevant [I]server.log[/I] section. Reports without these are asked for them once, then closed.
[*][B]"It doesn't work" is not a bug report.[/B] Tell me what you did, what you expected, and what actually happened.
[*][B]Unsupported:[/B] native Forge/NeoForge (use Arclight/Mohist), plugin conflicts I can't reproduce, general MC-server admin questions. Fabric is supported on a best-effort basis as an unstable frontier.
[*][B]Response time:[/B] solo maintainer. 24-72 h on weekdays for properly-filed reports. Critical safety issues (S-001 through S-007 violations) jump the queue.
[*][B]Feature requests[/B] via GitHub issues, not the resource thread. Priority follows the published roadmap, not ticket volume.
[/LIST]

This policy exists because focused engineering time is what keeps the plugin fast and current. Respecting it is how you get the most out of your purchase.
[/SPOILER]

